.SH SIGNALS
.TP
\f[B]SIGUSR1\f[R]
Triggers an immediate, zero\-flicker dynamic configuration and palette
reload.
The configuration file and all included palettes are reparsed, and GL
texture atlases and font faces are dynamically refreshed without
restarting the terminal or interrupting child processes.
.TP
\f[B]SIGWINCH\f[R]
Sent automatically to the child PTY foreground process group when the
Wayland surface resizes or font dimensions change.
.SH PROTOCOLS & EXTENSIONS
.TP
\f[B]Kitty Graphics Protocol\f[R]
Implements native Kitty graphics escape codes
(\f[CR]\(rsx1b_G...;payload\(rsx1b\(rs\f[R]).
Supports action types transmit (\f[CR]a=t\f[R]), transmit and display
(\f[CR]a=T\f[R]), query (\f[CR]a=q\f[R]), delete (\f[CR]a=d\f[R]), and
placement (\f[CR]a=p\f[R]).
Zero\-copy shared memory (\f[CR]t=s\f[R], \f[CR]t=f\f[R]) and direct
transmission (\f[CR]t=d\f[R], \f[CR]t=m\f[R]) modes are supported,
allowing seamless, high\-performance image display in tools like
\f[B]yazi(1)\f[R] and \f[B]image.nvim\f[R].
Responses are formatted strictly in compliance with the Kitty
specification.
.TP
\f[B]Wayland text\-input\-v3 (IME)\f[R]
Fully integrates Wayland \f[CR]zwp_text_input_v3\f[R] protocol for input
method engines such as \f[B]fcitx5(1)\f[R].
Accurately reports cursor rectangle coordinates in surface space to
position candidate popup windows, with native preedit text rendering and
styling.
.TP
\f[B]Kitty Keyboard Protocol\f[R]
Supports progressive keyboard enhancement modes (disambiguate escape
codes, report alternate keys, report all keys as escape sequences) to
eliminate legacy terminal escape ambiguities.
.TP
\f[B]OSC 52 Clipboard\f[R]
Supports reading and writing the system clipboard via standard OSC 52
base64 escape sequences.
.SH FILES
.TP
\f[CR]$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/ftty/ftty.toml\f[R] or \f[CR]\(ti/.config/ftty/ftty.toml\f[R]
Default user configuration file location.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
\f[B]FTTY_CONFIG\f[R]
Optional path to an alternative configuration file.
.TP
\f[B]TERM\f[R]
Terminal type identifier exported to child processes.
Set to \f[CR]xterm\-256color\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]COLORTERM\f[R]
Set to \f[CR]truecolor\f[R] to announce 24\-bit direct RGB color
capability.
.TP
\f[B]WAYLAND_DISPLAY\f[R]
Names the Wayland compositor socket used for connection.
